  "body": "A turning rough in a bar longer than the part now posts. Each pass that ends inside the bar's uncut end leaves its cut at feed instead of rapiding through it.\n\n### What was wrong\n\n- Each profile ride (`turning::prof::ride`) plunges in at the window's bottom, rides up the part, and leaves with a radial **rapid** out at the window's top.\n- When the bar runs on past that top (a bar longer than the part, or a window that stops partway along it), the nose sits inside the bar's uncut end when the pass ends. The rapid out crosses that stock.\n- The meridian law (#103) flagged it correctly: on `main` 0015347, the flanged bar from `turning_axial_rapids.rs` in a Ø20 bar 8 mm longer than the part gets 7 `RapidInStock` warnings, one per rung, and the post is refused.\n\n### What changed\n\n- `StockEnv` carries the bar's far end, `s_top`: the highest station the stock reaches along the part's axis. `operation::turning_stock::read` fills it from the stock in the part's own frame, the one the kernel walks.\n- `StockEnv::runs_past` says when the bar goes on past a ride's end (by more than `LONGER = 1e-6`, the same float-noise reading as `WIDER`).\n- `prof::ride` takes an `Exit`: `Rapid` as before, or `Feed` at the plunge feed (the ride's radial lead) out to the clear radius. Profile rough and profile finish pick it from the stock. The contour kinds (chamfer, taper, multi-pass) read no stock and keep `Rapid`.\n- A bar that ends with the part, or no readable stock, keeps the exact old path.\n- Facing already reads the bar's end (#122, merged), so this is the remaining half of the issue's \"done means\".\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/229-rough-bar-end.md` (always-feed and retract-along-the-cut were considered and dropped).\n\n### Tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/turning_axial_rapids.rs`: `a_rough_in_a_bar_longer_than_the_part_posts_clean`. This is the issue's pin: the job above generates with no `RapidInStock` and `posting::post_setup` writes the program. Fails on `main` with the 7 warnings above.\n- `crates/motion/tests/turning_stock.rs`:\n  - `a_pass_ending_inside_a_longer_bar_leaves_its_cut_at_feed`: rough and finish in a bar 8 mm longer. Every exit is a feed at the plunge feed, every move ends where it did in a bar the part's length, and that bar keeps rapid exits.\n  - `a_pass_stopping_partway_along_the_bar_leaves_its_cut_at_feed`: the window stops at Z 20 in a bar that runs to Z 28.\n- With `prof.rs` and its two contour callers put back to `main`, all three new tests fail, and the existing ones still pass.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local, built from upstream `main` 0015347 plus this commit)\n\n- `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick`: motion lib plus `turning_contour`, `turning_prof`, `turning_stock`; app lib plus `turning_axial_rapids`, `turning_stock_approach`. 265 tests, all pass.\n- Because a path change can move lathe goldens the gate map does not name, I also ran every lathe, turning and post suite by hand: 21 in app (`lathe_*`, `turning*`, `posting`, `fanuc_post`, `tormach_*`, `post_not_judged`), 6 in motion (`turning_blade`, `turning_bore`, `turning_face`, `turning_form`, `turning_thread`, `turning_thread_cycle`) and the sim's `stock_lathe`. 211 tests, all pass.\n\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The headless MCP has no way to load a lathe machine yet (#181), so the app-level check is the integration test above. It drives the real commands (set stock, load the lathe, add the tool, create and generate the op) and the real post. Not run on Linux or macOS.\n\nChangelog: A turning rough or finish in a bar longer than the part now leaves each pass at feed instead of rapiding through the bar's end, so the job posts (#229)\n\nFixes #229\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
